      "id": 1,
      "text": "Newburyport was officially incorporated in 1764 when the Massachusetts General Court split the original town of Newbury into a new seaport community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newburyport%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Merrimack River’s south bank, where Newburyport sits, was first inhabited by the Pawtucket Tribe before European settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.newburyportchamber.org/visitors-guide/history-of-newburyport/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The city’s historic waterfront still hosts the oldest operating bank in the United States, the Newburyport Five Cents Savings Bank, founded in 1854.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newburyport%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1740, English preacher George Whitefield visited Newburyport, inspiring the First Great Awakening with his powerful sermons.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newburyport%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "During the 1950s and 1960s, Newburyport’s downtown fell into disrepair, but a federal grant in 1970 saved most historic buildings from demolition.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newburyport%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Every August, the Newburyport Chamber Music Festival brings international artists to the town, offering free concerts and open rehearsals in historic homes.",
